                  },
                  "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Add an engine-level regression for nonpositive hysteresis**\n\nFor `fp16.hysteresis <= 0`, the user-visible fix is that ZeRO training can recover after overflow, but these tests invoke `update_scale()` directly and stub distributed rank. They never exercise configuration propagation, overflow detection, step skipping, or subsequent optimizer progress; the existing ZeRO overflow tests use positive hysteresis. Add a `DistributedTest` with `SimpleModel` through `deepspeed.initialize()` that verifies an overflowing step lowers the scale without updating weights, then a finite step updates weights for zero and negative hysteresis, and execute it on an fp16-capable device. Root `AGENTS.md` explicitly requires integration tests for training-loop contract changes and actual-device execution.\n\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L81-L82](https://github.com/deepspeedai/DeepSpeed/blob/35d643cee6cb7454f92bbcb95e191ba9a4f7714c/AGENTS.md#L81-L82)\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n<!-- codex-code-review-finding:v1 -->",
                  "createdAt": "2026-11-03T05:35:45Z",
                  "databaseId": 4451252811,
                  "diffHunk": "@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@\n+# Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation.\n+# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n+\n+# DeepSpeed Team\n+\n+import pytest\n+\n+from deepspeed.runtime.fp16.loss_scaler import DynamicLossScaler\n+\n+\n+@pytest.fixture(autouse=True)\n+def _patch_dist(monkeypatch):\n+    \"\"\"Stub out dist.get_rank so update_scale can run without a process group.\"\"\"\n+    import deepspeed.comm as dist\n+    monkeypatch.setattr(dist, \"get_rank\", lambda: 0)\n+\n+\n+INIT_SCALE = 2**16\n+SCALE_WINDOW = 1000\n+MIN_SCALE = 1\n+\n+\n+def _make_scaler(delayed_shift, consecutive_hysteresis=False):\n+    return DynamicLossScaler(\n+        init_scale=INIT_SCALE,\n+        scale_window=SCALE_WINDOW,\n+        min_scale=MIN_SCALE,\n+        delayed_shift=delayed_shift,\n+        consecutive_hysteresis=consecutive_hysteresis,\n+    )\n+\n+\n+class TestDynamicLossScalerHysteresis:\n+    \"\"\"Ensure DynamicLossScaler lowers its scale on overflow for all hysteresis values.\"\"\"\n+\n+    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"delayed_shift\", [0, -1, -5])\n+    def test_zero_or_negative_hysteresis_lowers_scale(self, delayed_shift):\n+        scaler = _make_scaler(delayed_shift)\n+        scaler.update_scale(overflow=True)\n+        assert scaler.cur_scale < INIT_SCALE",
